SPI Master 

- Purpose: Controls data communication between a microcontroller (Master) and peripheral devices (Slaves).
- Signals Used:- SCLK → SPI Clock (Synchronizes communication).
- MOSI → Master Out, Slave In (Sends data from Master).
- MISO → Master In, Slave Out (Receives data from Slave).
- CS → Chip Select (Activates the slave).


🔧 Functionality

- Master initiates communication by sending a clock signal (SCLK).
- MOSI transmits data from the Master.
- MISO receives data from the Slave (loopback used in your code).
- CS goes LOW when the Master selects a Slave.

🛠 Verilog Code Summary

- SPI Master Module- Generates clock (SCLK).
- Handles data flow (MOSI → MISO).
- Controls the slave using CS.

- Testbench- Toggles clk every 5 time units.
- Sends test data (mosi = 1, then mosi = 0).
- Ends simulation after testing.
